abstract_text:
[
  "The research domain of microbial mesoscale biology focuses on the evolution of multi-enzyme protein assemblies from complex operons and their production of specialized metabolites in uncultured microbial communities. Current analytical workflows rely heavily on biased reference databases restricted to culturable model organisms, creating a disconnect between uncultured metagenomic sequences and untargeted mass spectrometry data that leaves vast amounts of environmental genetic and metabolomic data hidden as unannotated biological dark matter. The primary objective is to construct a reference-free Genomic-to-Chemical Mesoscale Graph linking unannotated operons to their emergent biochemical phenotypes using a data-driven synthesis strategy involving deep learning and pattern-based mining. Datasets including raw sequence data from the Sequence Read Archive and MG-RAST alongside over 1.2 billion untargeted mass spectrometry spectra from GNPS and PRIDE will be synthesized using large-scale co-occurrence analyses and machine learning association models to integrate metadata from paired multi-omic studies. By shifting from reference-based observation to reference-free mapping of the genomic-to-chemical landscape, this research provides a significant contribution by enabling the discovery of unannotated biological dark matter."
]

